<div class="sec" id="s7">
  <div class="num">07</div>
  <h2>Cheat sheet</h2>
  <div class="cheat">
    <h3>Keep this for next time</h3>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Which window?</div>
        <p>
          <a href="#s5">Supplied request</a> (or optional Claude chat draft) → Claude
          Code plans → you approve → Claude Code builds → you inspect in the browser.
          <a href="/delta/index.html">Delta</a> is a separate assisted follow-up.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Start again</div>
        <p>
          Open a terminal, use <code>cd</code> to enter your project folder and run
          <code>claude --permission-mode plan</code>, not plain
          <code>claude</code>, which may start in Auto mode. Send your request,
          review the proposed plan, then approve it with Auto if available or
          manual approval. The Manual launch command is
          <code>claude --permission-mode default</code>; use <code>/plan</code>
          before each change. See <a href="#s3">setup</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Stop or finish</div>
        <p>
          Press Escape to interrupt Claude Code while it works. This does not
          undo completed changes; <code>/rewind</code> can undo its recent file edits.
          To end this local session, type
          <code>/exit</code> and press Enter.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">A new job</div>
        <p>
          Optionally use the <a href="#s4">prompt writer</a> for a substantial request.
          Prefix every new change with <code>/plan</code>, including small
          corrections in the existing conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Check the result</div>
        <p>
          Open <code>index.html</code>, refresh after edits and check the words,
          photos, image descriptions, email link and narrow layout. Use the <a
            href="#s5">website checks</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Recover</div>
        <p>
          Close the agents and keep the damaged folder. Make a fresh working
          copy of your last good backup with a new name. Continue in that copy;
          leave the backup untouched.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Publish, only if you choose</div>
        <p>
          Use the <a href="/publish/index.html">publishing follow-up</a> to prepare
          only public files and upload them yourself. Local edits do not update the
          live site. Never upload the whole project or a backup.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Safety</div>
        <p>
          No secrets. Read the plan and check the result. Keep backups outside
          every agent's working project. Auto mode is not bypass permissions or
          a safety guarantee; <a href="/delta/index.html"
            >Delta has different controls</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
